WEBVTT

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.510
Feelings (Continued)

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:40.470
A-Anti-bullying measures?!

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.020
Wh-What's wrong, Kiriyama?

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.270
Did something happen?

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:47.440
Tell me everything!

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.110
It's okay, Kiriyama!

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.780
No matter what happens, I'm on your side!

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.030
No, it's not about me.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.650
Really?

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.070
There's nothing you want to discuss?

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.030
Right now?

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.540
Of course not. In the first place...

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.290
...I'm not being bullied.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.130
I'm just being ignored.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.750
I don't have any friends. Or more like...

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:11.750
BLUNT

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.010
I'm not in anyone's field of vision.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:14.880
Kind of like that.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.300
SLAP

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.260
Well, never mind me.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:18.890
I'm a professional at that.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:22.640
After all, I've been eating lunch
by myself for over 11 years.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.260
SPARKLE

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.390
<i>Professional? In what?</i>

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.850
<i>Kiriyama!</i>

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.860
I see. A third-year middle school girl.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.990
In a family that's helped you out a lot, huh?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:41.620
First of all, it's a shame about that other girl
who switched schools.

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:43.370
But...

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:48.870
I think she was really lucky
to have someone like Hina.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:53.880
Otherwise, it could have had a sadder ending.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:02.140
Now, it's actually really important that Hina
was able to talk to her family about it.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.140
The worst thing anyone could do
is not talk about it, and keep it bottled up.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.440
Not talk to their family or their teacher...

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:17.900
But when it came to her friend, Chiho,
she told her homeroom teacher about it.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:22.280
But she got brushed off, apparently.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.580
The teacher said she was
"misreading the situation."

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.040
Dammit! So she's that type
of homeroom teacher, huh?

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.590
She got stuck with one of those. Poor kid.

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:37.050
She was probably desperate
when she asked for advice, too.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.130
I can get the teacher's perspective,

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.800
but that's no time to be running away!

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.100
So I thought I would ask your opinion
to get the school's perspective.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.220
UGH

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:43.850
JEEZ

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:44.850
UGH

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:45.600
JEEZ

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.390
UGH

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:47.310
JEEZ

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.560
I thought you could give me a hint
on how to handle this.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:50.980
S-Sorry.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.730
Kiriyama, look at this.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.110
BULLYING

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:55.690
School bullying problems getting worse!

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:55.690
Severe bullying. Please talk to us.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:04.370
If you do a search on "bullying,"
you'll get 89,100,000 hits.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.950
Do a search for "bullying countermeasures,"
and you get 2,200,000 hits.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:13.460
And nowhere in here is a solution
that'll work 100% of the time.

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:15.880
There.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.710
Take a look at this homepage.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.590
People who are being bullied.
People who are doing the bullying.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.840
The parents of both sides.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.810
People who saw it happen.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:30.140
People who were bullied in the past.
People who were bullies in the past.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:33.190
That teacher could scroll through
200 million pages

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:38.360
from several years and encounter
a mess of muddled arguments.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.780
The thing is, there are thousands
of sites like this.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:47.580
M-Mr. Hayashida? Mr. Hayashida...

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.710
But you won't find an answer in any of them.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.710
I mean, there's a distinct "answer"
for every one of these people here.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.500
It's a quandary.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:02.840
People who want an apology.

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.970
People who want to defend themselves.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.350
Parents who want to avenge their children.

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:09.430
Parents who want to clear
their children's names.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.430
People who want their bullies
to get the same treatment.

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.770
People who want to return
to their circle of friends.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:21.070
The configurations of the positions and
personalities of people involved are all different.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:27.070
That's why there's no "perfect answer"
that can work for every case.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.830
But that doesn't mean you should give up.

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:37.080
If you think, "there's no answer
to be found so I'll do nothing,"

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:40.090
...then you'll get nowhere.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:45.220
But at least we've come to know
what not to do.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.600
And that's to stir everyone up with cries of
"We have to solve this,"

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.520
while ignoring the victim's feelings,
and moving ahead too fast.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.400
<i>I say your daughter is the one who's lying!</i>

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.730
<i>My kid said she didn't do it!</i>

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.980
<i>Your daughter's obviously a delinquent!</i>

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:04.740
<i>She's tormented the hell out of my daughter!</i>

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:10.080
<i>Um, I've distributed surveys throughout
the school about whether bullying is going on.</i>

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.370
<i>- There's no need for that!
- You're going to pay for this.</i>

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.790
<i>No, stop! Stop! Please stop!</i>

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:22.750
If the victim doesn't want to make a big deal
out of it, or even get more people involved,

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:28.510
then it's wrong for the families to cause a commotion
at school, even if it solves the problem.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:32.140
<i>I heard she was bullied during second year.</i>

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:33.640
<i>Oh, really?</i>

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:36.430
<i>The whole school got involved.</i>

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:37.390
<i>Wow.</i>

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:43.530
Because even if the bullying died down,
if they feel out of place there,

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:44.900
then it was all for naught.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:54.660
So the important thing is to ask Hina
about what kind of solution she's hoping for.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.580
It's okay if this takes time,

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.290
so be sure to listen patiently
to all of her feelings on the matter.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:04.340
I see. Got it!

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.050
SCRIBBLE SCRIBBLE
NOTE NOTE

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:09.380
But actually, what's surprisingly effective
is being able to say "Stop it"

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:14.100
when the bully does something to them
right then and there.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:19.480
That all rides on whether
she's the type of person who can say that or not.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.480
Well...

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.690
Tell me about Hina.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.450
About Hina?

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.700
Hina, let's see.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.700
Um...

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.290
She's really energetic, with a loud voice...

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.130
Uh-huh. What else?

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:47.960
She laughs a lot,
and gets angry or dejected easily.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:49.970
You could say she's relatively complex.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:53.220
And pretty vain...

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:58.220
And for someone who's so cheerful,
she doesn't have much confidence in herself.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.150
But she's strong at heart. Very strong.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.070
<i>Kiriyama's been watching her closely, huh?</i>

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:07.400
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:09.650
<i>Could this be...</i>

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:11.530
<i>Could it possibly be...</i>

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.280
<i>...a flag?!</i>

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.410
H-Huh. You don't say.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:21.330
So, um... Uh, what?

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.920
I-Is she cute?

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.670
Yes, she's cute.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:31.930
Oh, I'm just asking for data purposes...

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:36.430
Um, so, in what way is she cute?

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:44.310
Uh, she has big eyes, small, thin arms and legs,
long, glossy hair...

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:51.150
CREAK

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:51.150
NERVOUS
NERVOUS

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:51.150
And then there's this,
to confirm, just in case...

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:52.900
Kiriyama...

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:58.660
Um, about that girl... How can I put this?

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.790
I-Is she important to you?

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:06.880
Yes. She's very important to me.

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.460
BLUNT

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:14.180
I intend to do anything I can for her.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.890
Diving into the atmosphere of adolescence!!

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.890
<i>Kiriyama!</i>

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:20.890
If she's in trouble,
I want to do anything I can to help.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:28.020
After all, she's my lifesaver.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:35.700
I have an obligation to pay her back.
That's my duty as a human being.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.990
Um, Kiriyama?

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:38.450
Kind of has a bad feeling about this

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:40.580
Whoa!

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:44.080
HOME TUTORING

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.080
Sorry, I got carried away there.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:47.000
No, no, you were fine.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:51.130
I was thrilled to see
a new side of you, Kiriyama...

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.340
HEAPS

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:54.760
280,000 per month x 9 months
Total 2,520,000

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.760
Say, Kiriyama.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:57.550
What is this?

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:02.020
Shishi-ou Tournament
Total
3,600,000 ~ 8,000,000

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:02.020
Um... And what's this?

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:06.850
It's a bracket for a shogi tournament, right?

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:14.030
And maybe all of these scrawled numbers are...

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:14.030
Total: 3,600,000-8,000,000

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.650
Total: 1,500,000

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.650
...money from matches?!

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:22.200
No, but since I was making a proposal,
and if I didn't hold it down to realistic figures,

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.290
it would just be irresponsible lip service.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:29.460
I have a debt to repay,
so I just can't be dreaming all day.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:32.880
Oh, good. My calculator still works.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:34.760
And so...

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:42.010
...from this point on,
I can't afford to lose any matches.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:43.520
Serious Eyes

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:46.180
<i>"I can't afford to lose any matches."</i>

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:52.270
Wood Carving

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:48.520
<i>Is that what you said without any hesitation?</i>

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.270
Oh, it's about time for my workshop.
I have to run!

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.280
Mr. Hayashida!

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:56.950
Thank you very much for your advice.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.820
It's given me food for thought.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:01.490
I would appreciate it
if we could talk again about this.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:02.700
<i>He's a little off.</i>

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.450
Well, excuse me!

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:09.460
<i>This kid is just off about something!</i>

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:14.380
<i>That's what the teacher's heart
was yelling out.</i>

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.010
<i>I have to check!</i>

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.260
<i>I have to put my life as a teacher on the line
and do something!</i>

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:26.270
<i>Before Kiriyama takes those documents
to her house and makes a speech!</i>

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:29.140
<i>Otherwise he's going to lose her!</i>

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:34.770
<i>Rei Kiriyama, 5th dan, 18 years old,
with calculator in hand, will intervene</i>

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.650
<i>in the life of that girl
to whom he owes a debt.</i>

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:41.030
Oh no! What am I going to do?!

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.160
<i>Would Hayashida,
his homeroom teacher from last year,</i>

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:46.870
<i>be able to stop him from running amok?</i>

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:49.790
<i>Stay tuned and you'll find out.</i>

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.040
Feelings

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.050
Confession

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:58.380
SHOGI HALL

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:00.340
Damn it!

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.350
What's wrong with Kiriyama?

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:09.810
I've never seen him this frustrated
after losing before!

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:10.350
Damn it.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:14.230
Finally...
Does he finally have the motivation?!

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:14.230
QUIVER QUIVER

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.440
Has he come around to the idea
of burning together

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.150
in the surging flames of passion?!

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:23.280
Kiriyama, welcome to the world
of bosom buddies!

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:23.910
GOOD

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:31.250
GRIND GRIND GRIND

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:26.620
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:31.250
<i>One more win and I would've gone to
the semifinals, where the pay gets doubled!</i>

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.710
<i>Damn it! I'm an idiot!</i>

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:36.960
GRIND GRIND GRIND

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.960
<i>Were you just talking big
about the debt repayment, Rei Kiriyama?!</i>

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:40.170
<i>If something happens
and she ends up going to another school,</i>

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:42.720
<i>or she stops going
and has to rely on private tutors,</i>

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.140
<i>or consults with a lawyer,
all of these things take money!</i>

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:51.480
<i>Whatever happens to Hina,
it's my job to prepare a place for her to go!</i>

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.650
Hey, Nikaidou! Are you here?

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.480
Oh! What is it, best friend?

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.820
I need to practice. Would you play me?

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.070
Of course, my best friend!

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.070
BEST FRIEND

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:07.950
I'm happy for you, Nikaidou!

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:08.950
GOOD

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:11.160
Is my place okay?

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.460
Anywhere works for me!

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:17.090
Wherever there's a board and pieces,
that's our battlefield, Kiriyama!

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:20.260
Ten matches with
a 30-minute time limit per move.

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:21.920
Don't fall behind, Nikaidou!

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:25.010
I can't lose at the next Kishousen Tournament.

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:28.930
MONEY DEBT MONEY
MONEY SHOGI MONEY

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:28.930
Inside Kiriyama's Brain

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.930
<i>In fact, I can't lose a single match!</i>

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.470
BEST FRIENDS BEST FRIENDS
BEST FRIENDS SHOGI BEST FRIENDS

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.470
Inside Nikaidou's Brain

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:31.470
<i>Kiriyama, those words are music to my ears!</i>

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.770
<i>It's tough. Everything is tough.</i>

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:37.480
<i>Reality is tough.</i>

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:41.740
<i>But that doesn't mean I can give up!</i>

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:49.870
<i>That's how it's been up to now,
and, of course, that's how it'll always be.</i>

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:54.160
<i>But right now, I'm doing it for Hina!</i>

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:05.630
<i>That Sunday, I got a text from Akari.</i>

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:08.760
POTATOES
ONIONS

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.760
Thanks, Kiriyama. This is a big help.

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:12.020
No, not at all. This is nothing.

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:15.020
They had so many special sales
to celebrate their remodeling.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:15.020
HEAVY

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:15.020
WOBBLE
WOBBLE...

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:18.480
I mean, just 200 yen
for a box of potatoes or onions.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.610
I couldn't pass that up, right?

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:23.440
And then there was 100 grams
of chicken thigh for 48 yen,

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:30.280
MARU S
SPECIAL SALE TODAY

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.650
99 yen for a tub of margarine,

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.820
100 grams of pork for 126 yen,

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:30.280
99 yen for a carton of milk...

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:33.240
Oh, I'm overjoyed!

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.120
Where's Hina today?

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:40.670
She's at the amusement park in Asakusa
with Grandpa and Momo.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:45.670
THREE LITTLE PIGS

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.670
She's still feeling a little down.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:46.720
Go!

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.680
So Grandpa took her there.

00:14:50.930 --> 00:14:53.470
I hope this will help her to feel better.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.980
Panda!

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:00.980
Hey, Kiriyama, are you okay with those?

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.480
Want me to take one?

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:05.650
I'm fine.

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:08.530
No problem.

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:14.580
Really? Are you sure they're not too heavy?
Don't overdo it.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:18.830
It's okay. I am a guy, after all.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.670
Rei doesn't seem to be getting fluffy at all.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:27.050
I worry about you.
How many kilos are you now?

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.550
My weight?

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:32.430
Um...

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:34.430
52 kg...

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:35.060
FREEZE

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:42.440
A-Akari?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.190
Um, please wait...

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.200
Thank you, Kiriyama.

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.950
Okay, then...

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.950
Well, I'll be on my way...

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:58.960
What are you talking about?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:00.710
Come in.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:05.340
Oh, but I'm always intruding...

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:08.760
HESITANT

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:08.760
<i>And it kind of seems like you're angry...</i>

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:10.510
What are you going on about?

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:15.350
You intend to make me break down
these vegetables by myself?

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:16.680
Help me!

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.100
R-Right!

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:24.610
Here. For starters,
peel the outer layer off of all these onions.

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:27.690
After that,
remove the strings from the string beans.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:28.940
Have you done it before?

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:31.400
Yes. I can do that.

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.580
I'm no good, huh?

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:50.090
<i>You didn't do a single thing wrong!</i>

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:52.090
<i>You helped your friend!</i>

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:53.970
<i>Be proud of yourself!</i>

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:00.600
Grandpa made a strong declaration like that,

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:04.310
but I...

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.230
<i>Hina...</i>

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:10.360
<i>Sis, what should I have done?</i>

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:14.660
I hesitated that time.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:19.950
I couldn't say something to Hina
like Grandpa did.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:25.540
Far from it. I asked her, "Why?"

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:29.210
"Why didn't you tell me this before?"

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:34.550
"Why couldn't you have handled it
more smoothly?"

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:36.680
"Why?"

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:40.390
Akari...

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:43.310
Grandpa told me this afterward.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:47.360
<i>I thought the same thing.</i>

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:51.940
<i>I think of the safety of a kid in my own family
before a kid in another family.</i>

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:55.610
<i>That's only natural. Everyone is that way.</i>

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:59.160
<i>But think about it.</i>

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.910
<i>Did Hina do anything wrong?</i>

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:03.660
<i>No, right?</i>

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:09.590
<i>Hina is suffering plenty as it is.</i>

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:20.100
<i>So if we ask her, "Why did you do that?"
on top of everything else, she'll feel lost.</i>

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:26.980
<i>More than anything,
shouldn't we praise Hina for her courage</i>

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:32.110
<i>and sense of justice for standing by her friend,
even though she knew</i>

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.570
<i>it might make her the next target?</i>

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:45.330
Ever since our Mom died,

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:50.460
I've been the surrogate mom
for Hina and Momo.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:55.840
I didn't know anything at 19.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:18:59.340
But Mom was counting on me.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.560
So I tried as hard as I could.

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:16.110
"Think about the people
who are around you, too."

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:19.110
"Be kind to people."

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:22.620
I've been pushing ham-fisted advice on her.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.960
But when push came to shove,
this is what happens.

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:37.380
I thought, "I don't care about justice.
I just wanted her to run away."

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:43.180
Even though Hina was hanging in there
for the sake of her friend,

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:45.720
I...

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:54.230
Akari...

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:58.530
You... You've got it wrong.

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:01.160
What you felt was normal.

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:05.160
No one wants a family member
to go through a painful experience.

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:09.370
After all, the one
who's been watching over Hina the most...

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:12.130
is you, Akari.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:21.840
I've been alone ever since I was a little kid.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:26.890
But the thought of someone extending
a helping hand was so terrifying.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:31.480
I couldn't ask for anyone's help.

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:37.650
But that day,
even though Hina said she was scared,

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:42.450
she was just as certain that she had "no regrets"
and "didn't do anything wrong."

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:46.410
It's like she was trying to convince herself.

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:51.120
At the time, I realized that she had saved me.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:55.710
That Hina was my savior...

00:20:56.210 --> 00:21:00.630
So you, who raised Hina to be a girl
with so much courage,

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:06.220
you're my savior too, Akari.

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:20.570
Is curry all right for dinner?

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:23.860
Yes.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.240
I should make a lot.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:32.210
I'm sure they'll come home hungry.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.420
We're home!

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:42.880
Guess what?! Pikatoo was there!

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:42.880
RAWRR

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:45.090
And I rode on a panda!

00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:48.140
Hey, wait, Momo!
You need to take your shoes off!

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:50.270
- Hold still now!
- Oh, it's Rei.

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:53.980
What the heck, kid? You're here today, too?

00:21:53.980 --> 00:21:55.480
Don't you visit too much?

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:57.690
I know!

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:58.860
I'll go home!

00:21:58.860 --> 00:22:00.190
Hey, Grandpa!

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:02.530
Don't take me seriously, idiot!

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:06.160
Pain in the neck. Eat, eat!

00:22:06.160 --> 00:22:07.490
That's right, Kiriyama.

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:09.990
Sorry.

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:12.040
Don't apologize!

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:14.500
You're making me look like a bad guy here!

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:22.010
Here.

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:25.260
I won it at a ball toss game.

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:28.180
I thought it looked like you.

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:32.810
I thought it might be childish, but...

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:43.780
No, I'm touched.

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:50.160
I love it!

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:52.410
Okay, wash your hands.

00:22:52.410 --> 00:22:54.250
Dinner's ready!

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:56.120
Okay!

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.040
Confession

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.970
Episode 28

00:24:33.640 --> 00:24:36.390
Cherries!

00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:39.680
Kiriyama came to have
instructional matches with us.

00:24:39.680 --> 00:24:41.690
It's called communicating, Kiriyama.

00:24:41.850 --> 00:24:45.070
Kiriyama, are you sure
that's all you want?

00:24:45.270 --> 00:24:50.030
Can you tell me about your school?
It can be about anything.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:58.500
ILLUSTRATION:
BUKUBU OHKAWA

00:24:50.650 --> 00:24:55.160
Kiriyama! I've been waiting
for you to become passionate!

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:57.830
I'll accompany you
until the very end!
